Z||000000||Richard Parnell||04-12-2001||02:24 PM||||Thanks Ogre, I did manage to salvage the old motors and mounted them in the older housings which were the same as the '87. I got the car back together, although I still need to make some adjustments to the body parts I replaced. The lights amazingly went up on the first try after aboout 5-7 tries on adjusting the hood. Had to "readjust w/5lb. hammer)" the bent portion of the frame that holds the hood hinge.<BR>I can tell now how much the front area of the car is bent. It's not too far off but unless I pull all the front and chain the car to a tree, it'll never be show quality with the car being perfect, but you know I just don't care. I just plain like my car, warts and all. I thought I'd be more upset about the wreck than I was. I actually had fun working on the car and it really wasn't that tough, unless you count getting up off your A** a chore, which I sometimes do. Well thanks for the advice. I do have some questions about the guages and some other electrical odd things that are happening on my car since I got rid of the ecm for the V8 conversion. <BR>Now I just need to sand the whole car down and get it painted, gold of course.<BR>||||reg||1
